  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool: scvi_n200 reaches 0.650 accuracy / 0.628 F1, clearly above pca_n2000 under the same profile and aggregation setting (0.591 / 0.573), while transformer aggregation was weaker for pca. This experiment tests whether the alternative RNA encoder scgpt can match or exceed scvi_n200 in the currently best setting, isolating the effect of representation choice. It is a one-factor extension of the most promising configuration, has high expected performance, and will clarify whether encoder selection is the next important lever before adding image fusion."
